  "description": "Arrival from the user list with a user pre-selected, which is the inherited TRIPLE-SEND path and the reason expectedResponse.sends is a list rather than a single screen. The NOT-REENTER arm finds CDEMO-CU02-USR-SELECTED non-blank at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:99-102, moves it into USRIDINI and performs PROCESS-ENTER-KEY. Inside that paragraph the read succeeds, so READ-USER-SEC-FILE's DFHRESP(NORMAL) arm at :334-339 sends once carrying 'Press PF5 key to save your updates ...' in DFHNEUTR; the second IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON at :166-172 then moves the four record fields onto the screen and sends AGAIN; and control returns to :105, whose unconditional PERFORM SEND-USRUPD-SCREEN sends a THIRD time. Three sends of the same map in one invocation is behaviour, not an artefact, and a translation that collapsed them would have changed what the terminal saw. The first send carries the fields as they stood before :167-170 ran - the user id moved in at :101 and the four fields blanked at :158-161.",
